# What `railway up` should NOT upload.
#
# Railway already honours .gitignore, so this file is only about things that ARE committed but
# that no Docker build stage reads. The upload is the slow part of `railway up`, and every file
# here is one the builder would receive, hash and then ignore.
#
# Nothing load-bearing is excluded. Dockerfile.backend now reads `backend/`, `deployments/` AND
# `frontend/` — it builds the observer UI into the API image so the whole protocol answers on one
# hostname. Everything listed below is read by neither image.

# Read-only historical reference. Never built, never deployed.
contractsv0/
backendv0/

# Solidity toolchain. The manifest and ABIs the backend needs live in deployments/, which is
# uploaded; the contracts source and its artifacts are not part of either image.
contracts/
agents/
tests/

# Documentation and planning.
docs/
*.md

# ...except the Agent Skill, which is SERVED at /skill rather than being documentation.
# The blanket *.md rule above silently keeps served markdown out of the image, and the endpoint
# then 404s in production while working perfectly in development. Anything served needs an
# exception here.
!backend/data/skill/*.md
LICENSE

# Moltbook: runs only as a local/manual process (`npm run moltbook:loop`), never inside the
# Railway-deployed backend. See docs/MOLTBOOK.md.
backend/src/integrations/moltbook/
backend/scripts/moltbook-*.ts
backend/test/moltbook.test.ts

# Local-only build output and caches, in case they are ever force-added.
**/dist/
**/artifacts/
**/cache/
**/coverage/
.git/
